//@version=6
// =============================================================================
// SaintTrades Top/Bottom Tick                                         INDICATOR
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Rejection-block top and bottom ticks. The rules come from:
//   GS    GSTRADES, "How To Top/Bottom Tick With REJECTION BLOCKS (FULL GUIDE)"
//   SH    Shinobi Signals, "My 1 Minute Top Tick Scalping Strategy"
//   PW    Powell (Dumb Money Concepts): wick CE model, key opens, CISD,
//         PXH/PXL daily bias, risk plan
//   ICT   ICT rejection block material: order flow, A+ criteria, SMT,
//         equal highs/lows
// Each rejection block (RB) gets a Gann box. A limit rests at its CE, and the
// chart prints TOP / BOT where that limit fills. Every fill is scored on 11
// confluences (12 with SMT), and the stats table measures the results.
// Non-repainting: everything runs on closed bars only.
//
// --------------------------------- RULES -------------------------------------
//  R1. An RB is the WICK of a candle on the RB timeframe that traded into a
//      higher-timeframe PD array or ran liquidity, then closed back away from
//      it. Bearish: the upper wick reaches the level and the body stays below
//      it. Bullish is the mirror image. (GS, SH, ICT)
//  R2. PD arrays are fair value gaps on two higher timeframes (1H and 4H by
//      default). The wick must reach the gap, and the body must not close past
//      its far edge. A gap dies when a chart bar closes through it. (GS, SH)
//  R3. Liquidity: previous day/week high and low, Asia / London / NY AM session
//      highs and lows, the previous 1H / 4H candle's high and low, swing points
//      on the RB timeframe, and the previous RB candle's high and low (SH; the
//      weakest). Key opens (18:00, 00:00, 09:30, 10:00, 13:00; optionally
//      02:00, 08:30, 13:30 New York) are two-sided, and a touch is enough. (PW)
//  R4. Gann box on the wick: 0 = tip, 0.25, 0.5 = CE, 1 = body edge. (GS)
//  R5. Entries. All four are measured on every RB:
//        0.5 CE       limit N ticks in front of the CE (SH 2-3, PW 2)
//        0.25         the deeper limit, also N ticks in front (GS)
//        1 body edge  fills on the first touch
//        CISD         after the first touch, enter on the first close back
//                     through the open of the push into the zone (PW)
//  R6. Stop: past the tip plus a buffer (GS, PW "stop above the wick"), or a
//      fixed size in points (PW 5/10-point stops). The RB is invalid once a
//      wick trades past 0. (GS)
//  R7. Targets: TP1 = fixed R. TP2 = fixed R, the nearest untaken opposing
//      liquidity (GS), or the midnight / true day open (PW).
//  R8. Score. Setup factors, known when the RB candle closes:
//        PD array    the wick traded into an HTF fair value gap (SH: higher
//                    odds than a plain sweep)
//        Liquidity   the wick ran key liquidity or a key open
//        P/D         shorts above / longs below the midnight and 18:00 opens
//                    (GS, SH, PW)
//        Bias        Powell's PXH/PXL daily bias agrees
//        Order flow  the last swing broken on the PD-array timeframe agrees.
//                    ICT: trade RBs with order flow.
//        Clean tip   the tip makes no equal highs/lows (wick theory)
//        SMT         the comparison symbol failed to make the same new high/low
//      Entry factors, known when the limit fills:
//        Engineered liquidity  a swing formed after the RB between the body
//                    edge (less a quarter wick) and the entry, and the move
//                    into the entry ran it (PW: liquidity right below the CE)
//        LTF gap     the entry sits inside an unfilled chart-timeframe gap (SH)
//        OTE         the entry is a 62-79% retracement of the leg from the
//                    tip to the extreme made after the RB, once that leg
//                    runs past the RB candle's own range (SH)
//        Displaced   a CISD close (PW), or an inverted chart-timeframe gap
//                    from the leg into the tip (GS), printed before the fill
//        Session     the fill came inside the New York session (GS)
//      Grade = score / max: A+ at 75% or more, A at 62%, B at 50%, else C.
//  R9. Daily risk plan (PW): the first trade is full size, and a win ends the
//      day. After a loss the next trade is half size, then a quarter. The day
//      ends after the last allowed trade.
//
// ------------------------------- ASSUMPTIONS ---------------------------------
//  A1. RB-timeframe and gap-timeframe candles are built from chart bars. A
//      candle is finalized on its last chart bar. If that bar can't be detected
//      (a session break), it is finalized on the next bar instead. Such an RB
//      can't fill on that bar, and it is dropped if that bar already took its
//      tip.
//  A2. A level or gap counts only if it existed before the RB candle opened. A
//      one-sided level also must not have been traded through before then. A
//      gap closed through during the RB candle still counts for that candle.
//  A3. Key opens need a chart bar that opens at that exact minute. They expire
//      when the New York trading day rolls at 18:00.
//  A4. One RB per zone: a wick inside a live RB of the same direction is a
//      retest of that RB, not a new one.
//  A5. Fills are conservative. A limit fills from the bar after the RB is
//      known. Its targets count from the bar after the fill, and a stop on the
//      fill bar counts. A limit is cancelled if the RB is invalidated or
//      expires, or if price reaches its TP2 before it fills. A CISD entry fills
//      at the trigger close.
//  A6. Entry factors use only what was known before the fill bar: swings
//      confirmed and gaps formed on earlier bars, and the leg extreme up to
//      the previous bar.
//  A7. Stats count RBs whose four entries have all resolved. "→TP1" holds the
//      whole position to TP1 and "→TP2" to TP2, with the same stop and no
//      breakeven. A win is R > 0, and avg R is per filled trade.
//  A8. Daily bias (PW PXH/PXL), from the last completed daily candle against
//      the one before it:
//        close above that day's high                   bullish
//        close below its low                           bearish
//        took only its high and closed back inside     bearish
//        took only its low and closed back inside      bullish
//        inside or outside day                         the candle's color
//      Order flow = the direction of the last close through a 3-candle swing
//      on gap timeframe A (B if A is off).
//  A9. The daily plan uses the selected entry's fills at or above the minimum
//      grade, one trade at a time, on the New York trading day (rolls at
//      18:00). A trade's result belongs to the day it was taken.
// =============================================================================

indicator("SaintTrades Top/Bottom Tick", "ST TBT", overlay=true, max_boxes_count=500, max_lines_count=500, max_labels_count=500)

// ============================== TYPES ========================================
type Lvl
    float  price
    string name
    int    kind            // 0 = key open (two-sided), 1 = high-side liquidity, -1 = low-side liquidity
    int    tier            // 3 = day/week, 2 = key open / session / HTF candle, 1 = swing
    int    bornT           // earliest RB-candle open time that may use this level (A2)
    int    takenT          // first chart bar that traded through it (one-sided only)
    int    deadT           // replaced by a newer level of the same name at this time
    int    dayId
    int    bornBar
    line   ln
    label  lb

type Gap
    bool   bull
    float  top
    float  bot
    string name
    int    bornT           // earliest RB-candle open time that may use this gap (A2)
    int    left
    int    invT            // chart bar that closed through it
    box    bx

type Agg
    float o
    float h
    float l
    float c
    int   bar
    bool  done = true
    array<float> H
    array<float> L
    array<int>   B

type Trade
    float entry
    float stop
    float tp1
    float tp2
    float risk
    bool  tapped    = false
    int   tapBar
    float ext
    int   extBar
    float cisd
    bool  filled    = false
    int   fillBar
    bool  cancelled = false
    bool  done1     = false
    bool  done2     = false
    float r1        = 0.0
    float r2        = 0.0
    int   score     = 0
    bool  fEl       = false
    bool  fLtf      = false
    bool  fOte      = false
    bool  fDisp     = false
    bool  fNy       = false
    float size      = 0.0
    bool  boxDone   = false
    box   pW
    box   pL
    label lbT
    label lbE
    label lbS

type RB
    bool   bull
    float  tip
    float  edge
    float  ce
    float  q25
    string names
    int    formT
    int    formBar
    int    tipBar
    int    legBar
    int    trackFrom
    int    fillFrom
    int    age       = 0
    float  cisdLvl
    int    dispCount = 0
    bool   disp      = false
    string dispBy    = ""
    bool   tapped    = false
    bool   invalid   = false
    bool   expired   = false
    bool   resolved  = false
    bool   zoneDone  = false
    float  far             // the RB candle's opposite extreme
    float  ext             // the leg's extreme since the RB closed (OTE)
    int    sScore    = 0
    bool   fPda      = false
    bool   fLiq      = false
    bool   fPd       = false
    bool   fBias     = false
    bool   fOf       = false
    bool   fClean    = false
    bool   fSmt      = false
    Trade  t0
    Trade  t1
    Trade  t2
    Trade  t3
    box    bx
    line   ceLn
    line   qLn
    label  tag
    line   lnE
    line   lnS
    line   lnT1
    line   lnT2
    label  lbE
    label  lbS
    label  lbT1
    label  lbT2

type State
    float atr
    int   ofDir = 0
    float swH
    float swL

// =============================== INPUTS ======================================
G_RB  = "1 · Rejection block"
G_PD  = "2 · Where RBs form"
G_TR  = "3 · Entry, stop & targets"
G_CF  = "4 · Score & filters"
G_PL  = "5 · Daily risk plan (Powell)"
G_VIS = "6 · Visuals"
G_ST  = "7 · Stats"

rbTfIn      = input.string("15m", "RB timeframe", options=["Chart", "1m", "3m", "5m", "15m", "30m", "1H", "4H"], tooltip="The candle whose wick is the rejection block. GS reads it on the 5m/15m, Shinobi on the 15m and up (1H/4H preferred), Powell on the 4H/1H/15m. A timeframe below the chart's falls back to the chart.", group=G_RB)
zoneFrom    = input.string("Body edge", "Zone runs from", options=["Body edge", "Close"], tooltip="Body edge = the wick only (GS: mark the wick, not the body). Close = from the close to the tip.", group=G_RB)
minWickPct  = input.float(40.0, "Rejecting wick ≥ % of candle range", minval=0, maxval=100, step=5, group=G_RB)
minWickBody = input.float(1.0, "Rejecting wick ≥ body ×", minval=0, step=0.25, group=G_RB)
minWickAtr  = input.float(0.25, "Rejecting wick ≥ ATR(14) ×", minval=0, step=0.05, tooltip="ATR of the RB timeframe. Ignores small wicks. 0 = off.", group=G_RB)
maxWickAtr  = input.float(0.0, "Rejecting wick ≤ ATR(14) × (0 = off)", minval=0, step=0.5, tooltip="ICT: very long wicks (news spikes) tend to get filled completely instead of holding.", group=G_RB)
invMode     = input.string("Wick past tip", "Invalidate when", options=["Wick past tip", "Close past tip"], tooltip="GS: once the tip at 0 is run, the RB is invalid.", group=G_RB)
rbLife      = input.int(12, "RB life (RB candles, 0 = no limit)", minval=0, maxval=500, tooltip="ICT: recent RBs that get tapped quickly hold best. Unfilled entries are cancelled after this many RB-timeframe candles.", group=G_RB)
swingN      = input.int(8, "Tip must be the high / low of the last N RB candles", minval=0, maxval=100, tooltip="Only wicks that are the swing extreme (8 candles = 2 hours on the 15m) count, so arrows sit on real tops and bottoms instead of mid-range wicks. 0 = off.", group=G_RB)
dispWin     = input.int(6, "CISD displacement window (RB candles)", minval=1, maxval=50, tooltip="How many RB candles after the RB may close through the open of the push into it and still count as displacement.", group=G_RB)

pdaAIn   = input.string("1H", "HTF gaps · timeframe A", options=["Off", "30m", "1H", "2H", "4H", "D"], tooltip="GS: the wick must trade into a 1H-or-higher PD array, mostly fair value gaps. Shinobi: 4H/1H gaps. Timeframe A also sets order flow.", group=G_PD)
pdaBIn   = input.string("4H", "HTF gaps · timeframe B", options=["Off", "30m", "1H", "2H", "4H", "D"], group=G_PD)
fvgMinTk = input.int(4, "HTF gap minimum size (ticks)", minval=1, maxval=4000, group=G_PD)
fvgKeep  = input.int(6, "HTF gaps kept per timeframe & side", minval=1, maxval=30, group=G_PD)
useKO    = input.bool(true, "Powell key opens (New York time)", group=G_PD)
ko1800   = input.bool(true, "18:00", inline="ko1", group=G_PD)
ko0000   = input.bool(true, "00:00", inline="ko1", group=G_PD)
ko0200   = input.bool(false, "02:00", inline="ko1", group=G_PD)
ko0830   = input.bool(false, "08:30", inline="ko1", tooltip="Powell: 08:30 matters only on news days. 13:00 starts the PM session.", group=G_PD)
ko0930   = input.bool(true, "09:30", inline="ko2", group=G_PD)
ko1000   = input.bool(true, "10:00", inline="ko2", group=G_PD)
ko1300   = input.bool(true, "13:00", inline="ko2", group=G_PD)
ko1330   = input.bool(false, "13:30", inline="ko2", group=G_PD)
usePD    = input.bool(true, "Previous day high / low", group=G_PD)
usePW    = input.bool(true, "Previous week high / low", group=G_PD)
useSes   = input.bool(true, "Session highs / lows: Asia 20-00, London 02-05, NY AM 09:30-12", group=G_PD)
useHtfC  = input.bool(true, "Previous HTF candle high / low (timeframes A and B)", tooltip="Powell: the 4H wick swept the previous 4H high.", group=G_PD)
useSw    = input.bool(false, "Swing highs / lows on the RB timeframe", group=G_PD)
swLen    = input.int(3, "Swing strength (candles each side)", minval=1, maxval=10, group=G_PD)
swKeep   = input.int(10, "Swing levels kept per side", minval=1, maxval=30, group=G_PD)
usePrev  = input.bool(false, "Previous RB candle high / low (Shinobi)", tooltip="A wick that sweeps the candle before it and closes back. The weakest trigger: it doesn't earn the liquidity point.", group=G_PD)
sweepTk  = input.int(1, "Liquidity sweep: min ticks through", minval=0, maxval=100, tooltip="How far a wick must trade past a high or low to count as a sweep. Key opens and gaps only need a touch.", group=G_PD)
smtSym   = input.string("", "SMT symbol (blank = off)", tooltip="A correlated symbol, e.g. CME_MINI:ES1! on an NQ chart or CME_MINI:NQ1! on ES. SMT holds when this chart's RB candle makes a new high (low) over the lookback and the other symbol's candle doesn't.", group=G_PD)
smtLook  = input.int(10, "SMT lookback (RB candles)", minval=2, maxval=50, group=G_PD)

entrySel = input.string("0.5 CE", "Entry shown & alerted", options=["0.5 CE", "0.25", "1 body edge", "CISD after tap"], tooltip="0.5 CE = limit at the wick's 50% (GS, Shinobi, Powell). 0.25 = the deeper limit near the tip, better price but fewer fills (GS). 1 = first touch of the body edge. CISD = market entry on the first close back through the open of the push into the zone. The stats table measures all four either way.", group=G_TR)
frontTk  = input.int(2, "Front-run the limit by (ticks)", minval=0, maxval=40, tooltip="Shinobi: set the limit 2-3 ticks in front of the CE so it fills when price stops just short. Powell allows 2 ticks for spread. Applies to the 0.5 and 0.25 limits.", group=G_TR)
stopMode = input.string("Past the tip", "Stop", options=["Past the tip", "Fixed points"], group=G_TR)
stopTk   = input.int(4, "Stop buffer past the tip (ticks)", minval=0, maxval=400, tooltip="GS: a little past the high, not exactly at it, because the market likes to run it. 4 ticks = 1 NQ point.", group=G_TR)
stopPts  = input.float(10.0, "Fixed stop (points)", minval=0.25, step=0.25, tooltip="Powell: 5 or 10-point stops on the wick CE (10 preferred).", group=G_TR)
maxStop  = input.float(0.0, "Skip RBs whose 0.5 stop is wider than (points, 0 = off)", minval=0, step=0.25, tooltip="For prop accounts. GS runs about 50 ticks (12.5 NQ points); Shinobi about 10 points.", group=G_TR)
tp1R     = input.float(1.0, "TP1 (R)", minval=0.25, step=0.25, group=G_TR)
tp2Mode  = input.string("Opposing liquidity", "TP2", options=["Fixed R", "Opposing liquidity", "Midnight open"], tooltip="Opposing liquidity = the nearest untaken high (longs) or low (shorts) beyond TP1 (GS). Midnight open = true day open (Powell), when it lies beyond TP1. Both fall back to the fixed R.", group=G_TR)
tp2R     = input.float(3.0, "TP2 (R)", minval=0.5, step=0.25, group=G_TR)
cisdWin  = input.int(12, "CISD entry: bars allowed after the tap", minval=1, maxval=300, group=G_TR)
flat16   = input.bool(true, "16:00 NY: cancel unfilled entries, close trades, expire RBs", group=G_TR)

minGrade = input.string("B", "TOP / BOT, alerts & stats from grade", options=["A+", "A", "B", "C"], tooltip="Grade = score / max score: A+ ≥ 75%, A ≥ 62%, B ≥ 50%, C below. Fills under this grade get no marker or alert, and they are left out of the entry rows and the daily plan. The filter lab still measures every fill.", group=G_CF)
minSetup = input.int(0, "Hide RBs with a setup score below", minval=0, maxval=7, group=G_CF)
reqPda   = input.bool(false, "Require an HTF gap (PD array)", group=G_CF)
reqLiq   = input.bool(false, "Require key level / liquidity", group=G_CF)
reqPd    = input.bool(false, "Require premium (shorts) / discount (longs)", group=G_CF)
reqBias  = input.bool(false, "Require daily bias", group=G_CF)
reqOf    = input.bool(false, "Require order flow", group=G_CF)
reqClean = input.bool(false, "Require clean tip", group=G_CF)
pdMode   = input.string("Midnight + 18:00 open", "Premium / discount vs", options=["Midnight + 18:00 open", "Midnight open"], tooltip="GS buys under both the midnight and the 18:00 open. Shinobi and Powell use the midnight (true day) open. Before midnight, the 18:00 open stands in.", group=G_CF)
eqTk     = input.int(4, "Clean tip: equal high/low tolerance (ticks)", minval=0, maxval=400, group=G_CF)
eqLook   = input.int(20, "Clean tip: lookback (RB candles)", minval=2, maxval=50, group=G_CF)
elStr    = input.int(2, "Engineered liquidity: swing strength (chart bars)", minval=1, maxval=10, tooltip="Powell: liquidity engineered just below the CE, then run into it. A chart-timeframe swing that formed after the RB, between the body edge (less a quarter of the wick) and the entry.", group=G_CF)
ltfMinTk = input.int(2, "LTF gap minimum size (ticks)", minval=1, maxval=400, group=G_CF)
oteLo    = input.float(0.62, "OTE from", minval=0, maxval=1, step=0.01, inline="ote", group=G_CF)
oteHi    = input.float(0.79, "to", minval=0, maxval=1, step=0.01, inline="ote", group=G_CF)
nySess   = input.string("0830-1600", "Session (New York, HHMM-HHMM)", tooltip="GS: rejection blocks work best in the New York session.", group=G_CF)
reqSess  = input.bool(true, "Only take trades that fill inside the session", group=G_CF)

planOn   = input.bool(true, "Daily risk plan: one trade at a time", tooltip="Powell: trade 1 full size; a win ends the day. After a loss, trade 2 at half size; after another, trade 3 at a quarter. Then the day is over. Only trades the plan takes get an arrow and a box. Off = every qualifying fill is shown.", group=G_PL)
planMax  = input.int(2, "Max trades per day", minval=1, maxval=5, group=G_PL)
planTgt  = input.string("TP2", "Trades exit at (boxes & plan)", options=["TP1", "TP2"], group=G_PL)

style    = input.string("Clean", "Style", options=["Clean", "Detailed"], tooltip="Clean = an arrow on the wick that was traded plus a TradingView-style position box (green = target, red = stop). Detailed = RB boxes, Gann lines and TOP / BOT labels.", group=G_VIS)
colTopA  = input.color(#f23645, "Top arrow", inline="c0", group=G_VIS)
colBotA  = input.color(#2962ff, "Bottom arrow", inline="c0", group=G_VIS)
colBull  = input.color(#26a69a, "Bullish", inline="c1", group=G_VIS)
colBear  = input.color(#ef5350, "Bearish", inline="c1", group=G_VIS)
colFvg   = input.color(#9598a1, "HTF gaps", inline="c2", group=G_VIS)
colKO    = input.color(#b2b5be, "Key opens", inline="c2", group=G_VIS)
colLiq   = input.color(#787b86, "Liquidity", inline="c2", group=G_VIS)
colEnt   = input.color(#2962ff, "Entry", inline="c3", group=G_VIS)
colSl    = input.color(#ef5350, "Stop", inline="c3", group=G_VIS)
colTp    = input.color(#26a69a, "Targets", inline="c3", group=G_VIS)
showFvg  = input.bool(false, "Draw live HTF gaps", group=G_VIS)
showGann = input.bool(true, "Gann levels 0.25 and 0.5 (CE)", group=G_VIS)
drawKO   = input.bool(false, "Draw today's key opens", group=G_VIS)
drawLiq  = input.bool(false, "Draw untaken liquidity", group=G_VIS)
lblMode  = input.string("Compact", "RB labels", options=["Compact", "Full", "Off"], tooltip="Compact = direction, setup score and ✓ once displaced, e.g. ▼ 4/6 ✓. Full also lists what the wick ran. Hover a label for the Gann levels and the factors.", group=G_VIS)
keepLbl  = input.bool(false, "Keep labels on finished RBs", group=G_VIS)
maxKeep  = input.int(8, "RBs kept on the chart", minval=1, maxval=100, group=G_VIS)
markKeep = input.int(150, "Trades kept on the chart", minval=1, maxval=400, group=G_VIS)
lvlN     = input.int(0, "Entry / stop / TP lines for the newest N live RBs", minval=0, maxval=5, group=G_VIS)

tblMode  = input.string("Off", "Stats table", options=["Compact", "Full", "Off"], tooltip="Compact = context, the four entries and the daily plan. Full adds the filter lab.", group=G_ST)
statsPos = input.string("Top Right", "Table position", options=["Top Right", "Top Left", "Bottom Right", "Bottom Left", "Middle Right"], group=G_ST)

// ============================= CONSTANTS =====================================
NY      = "America/New_York"
TICK    = syminfo.mintick
MAX_AGE = 4500      // TradingView refuses drawings anchored ~10,000 bars back

tfOf(string s) =>
    switch s
        "1m"  => "1"
        "3m"  => "3"
        "5m"  => "5"
        "15m" => "15"
        "30m" => "30"
        "1H"  => "60"
        "2H"  => "120"
        "4H"  => "240"
        "D"   => "D"
        => timeframe.period

tfName(string tf) =>
    int s = timeframe.in_seconds(tf)
    s >= 86400 ? str.tostring(math.round(s / 86400.0)) + "D" : s >= 3600 ? str.tostring(math.round(s / 3600.0)) + "H" : s >= 60 ? str.tostring(math.round(s / 60.0)) + "m" : str.tostring(s) + "s"

sessMin(string s, int k) =>
    int(str.tonumber(str.substring(s, k, k + 2))) * 60 + int(str.tonumber(str.substring(s, k + 2, k + 4)))

rbTfSel = tfOf(rbTfIn)
rbTf    = rbTfIn != "Chart" and rbTfSel != timeframe.period and timeframe.in_seconds(rbTfSel) > timeframe.in_seconds() ? rbTfSel : timeframe.period
onA     = pdaAIn != "Off"
onB     = pdaBIn != "Off"
tfA     = onA ? tfOf(pdaAIn) : timeframe.period
tfB     = onB ? tfOf(pdaBIn) : timeframe.period
rbName  = tfName(rbTf)
nameA   = tfName(tfA)
nameB   = tfName(tfB)
smtOn   = smtSym != ""
smtTk   = smtOn ? smtSym : syminfo.tickerid
nyS     = sessMin(nySess, 0)
nyE     = sessMin(nySess, 5)
selIdx  = entrySel == "0.5 CE" ? 0 : entrySel == "0.25" ? 1 : entrySel == "1 body edge" ? 2 : 3
invWick = invMode == "Wick past tip"
fixStop = stopMode == "Fixed points"
SETUPMAX = smtOn ? 7 : 6
MAXS     = SETUPMAX + 5
showStats = tblMode != "Off"
fullTbl   = tblMode == "Full"
clean     = style == "Clean"
var ENTRY_NAMES = array.from("0.5 CE", "0.25", "1 body edge", "CISD after tap")

// ============================== STATE ========================================
var State      S    = State.new()
var array<Lvl> lvls = array.new<Lvl>()
var array<RB>  rbs  = array.new<RB>()
var array<Gap> gaps = array.new<Gap>()
var Agg        AA   = Agg.new(H=array.new<float>(), L=array.new<float>(), B=array.new<int>())
var Agg        AB   = Agg.new(H=array.new<float>(), L=array.new<float>(), B=array.new<int>())

// closed RB-timeframe candles, oldest first (hSH / hSL = the SMT symbol's candle)
var array<float> hO  = array.new<float>()
var array<float> hH  = array.new<float>()
var array<float> hL  = array.new<float>()
var array<float> hC  = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   hB  = array.new<int>()
var array<float> hSH = array.new<float>()
var array<float> hSL = array.new<float>()

// chart-timeframe gaps and confirmed swings (entry factors, A6)
var array<bool>  lgBull = array.new<bool>()
var array<float> lgTop  = array.new<float>()
var array<float> lgBot  = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   lgBar  = array.new<int>()
var array<float> pvH    = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   pvHB   = array.new<int>()
var array<float> pvL    = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   pvLB   = array.new<int>()

// stats per entry (0 = 0.5 CE, 1 = 0.25, 2 = body edge, 3 = CISD) and filter-lab rows
var array<int>   eFill = array.new<int>(4, 0)
var array<float> eS1   = array.new<float>(4, 0.0)
var array<int>   eW1   = array.new<int>(4, 0)
var array<float> eS2   = array.new<float>(4, 0.0)
var array<int>   eW2   = array.new<int>(4, 0)
LAB_N = 17
var array<int>   lN  = array.new<int>(LAB_N, 0)
var array<float> lS1 = array.new<float>(LAB_N, 0.0)
var array<int>   lW1 = array.new<int>(LAB_N, 0)
var array<float> lS2 = array.new<float>(LAB_N, 0.0)
var array<int>   lW2 = array.new<int>(LAB_N, 0)
var int setups = 0
var array<label> marks = array.new<label>()
var array<Trade> boxedT = array.new<Trade>()

// day / week / session context
var float dO       = na
var float dH       = na
var float dL       = na
var float pdH      = na
var float pdL      = na
var int   bias     = 0
var float wH       = na
var float wL       = na
var float mOpen    = na
var int   mOpenDay = -1
var int   koDay    = 0      // New York trading day, rolls at 18:00 (A3)
var float koOpen   = na     // the 18:00 open
var bool  sawEve   = false  // the symbol trades at/after 18:00 NY
var float asH = na
var float asL = na
var float lnH = na
var float lnL = na
var float nyH = na
var float nyL = na
var bool  inAs = false
var bool  inLn = false
var bool  inNy = false

// chart-bar runs for the CISD trigger: open of the first bar of the current up/down-close run
var float upRun = na
var float dnRun = na

// RB-timeframe candle being built (aSH / aSL = SMT symbol)
var float aO    = na
var float aH    = na
var float aL    = na
var float aC    = na
var float aSH   = na
var float aSL   = na
var int   aT    = na
var int   aBar  = na
var int   aHB   = na
var int   aLB   = na
var bool  aDone = true

// daily risk plan (R9, A9)
var int   planDay   = -1
var int   dayTrades = 0
var bool  dayDone   = false
var float dayR      = 0.0
var Trade planT     = na
var int   planDays  = 0
var int   planWinD  = 0
var float planR     = 0.0
var int   planN     = 0
var int   planW     = 0

// ============================ PER-BAR SERIES =================================
// Called on every bar so their history stays consistent; used on confirmed bars only.
nyMin(int t) =>
    hour(t, NY) * 60 + minute(t, NY)

bool chgRb     = timeframe.change(rbTf)
int  tcRb      = time_close(rbTf)
bool newRbBar  = rbTf == timeframe.period or chgRb
bool lastRbBar = rbTf == timeframe.period or (not na(tcRb) and time_close == tcRb)
bool useA      = tfA != timeframe.period and timeframe.in_seconds(tfA) > timeframe.in_seconds()
bool chgA      = timeframe.change(tfA)
int  tcA       = time_close(tfA)
bool newABar   = not useA or chgA
bool lastABar  = not useA or (not na(tcA) and time_close == tcA)
bool useB      = tfB != timeframe.period and timeframe.in_seconds(tfB) > timeframe.in_seconds()
bool chgB      = timeframe.change(tfB)
int  tcB       = time_close(tfB)
bool newBBar   = not useB or chgB
bool lastBBar  = not useB or (not na(tcB) and time_close == tcB)
bool newDay    = timeframe.change("D")
bool newWeek   = timeframe.change("W")
int  mNow      = nyMin(time)
int  mCls      = na(time_close) ? na : nyMin(time_close)
int  nyDom     = dayofmonth(time, NY)
bool newNyDate = na(nyDom[1]) or nyDom != nyDom[1]
int  mPrv      = mNow[1]
bool cross18   = not na(mPrv) and mNow >= 1080 and (mPrv < 1080 or time - time[1] >= 43200000)
bool flatNow   = flat16 and not na(mCls) and mNow < 960 and mCls >= 960
float pvhNow   = ta.pivothigh(high, elStr, elStr)
float pvlNow   = ta.pivotlow(low, elStr, elStr)
[smtH, smtL]   = request.security(smtTk, timeframe.period, [high, low])

// ============================== HELPERS ======================================
gradeOf(int s, int mx) =>
    float p = mx > 0 ? float(s) / mx : 0.0
    p >= 0.75 ? "A+" : p >= 0.62 ? "A" : p >= 0.5 ? "B" : "C"

gRank(string g) =>
    g == "A+" ? 3 : g == "A" ? 2 : g == "B" ? 1 : 0

gRankMin = gRank(minGrade)

passes(Trade t) =>
    gRank(gradeOf(t.score, MAXS)) >= gRankMin

f_pct(int a, int b) =>
    b > 0 ? str.tostring(math.round(100.0 * a / b)) + "%" : "-"

// average R and win rate, e.g. "+0.42R · 55%"
fR(float sum, int wins, int n) =>
    n > 0 ? (sum / n >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(sum / n, "0.00") + "R · " + str.tostring(math.round(100.0 * wins / n)) + "%" : "-"

fRs(float r) =>
    (r >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(r, "0.00") + "R"

isDone(Trade t) =>
    t.cancelled or (t.filled and t.done1 and t.done2)

trd(RB r, int m) =>
    m == 0 ? r.t0 : m == 1 ? r.t1 : m == 2 ? r.t2 : r.t3

yes(bool b) =>
    b ? "✓" : "✗"

px(float p) =>
    str.tostring(p, format.mintick)

// A level is born (R3). Key opens are dotted, liquidity dashed.
addLvl(float p, string n, int k, int tier, int bt, int d) =>
    Lvl lv = Lvl.new(price=p, name=n, kind=k, tier=tier, bornT=bt, dayId=d, bornBar=bar_index)
    if k == 0 ? drawKO : drawLiq
        color c = k == 0 ? colKO : colLiq
        lv.ln := line.new(bar_index, p, bar_index + 1, p, color=color.new(c, 30), style=k == 0 ? line.style_dotted : line.style_dashed, width=1)
        lv.lb := label.new(bar_index, p, n, color=color.new(color.black, 100), style=label.style_label_lower_left, textcolor=c, size=size.tiny)
    array.push(lvls, lv)
    true

dropLvl(int i) =>
    Lvl lv = array.get(lvls, i)
    line.delete(lv.ln)
    label.delete(lv.lb)
    array.remove(lvls, i)
    true

// A new level replaces the previous one of the same name. The old one stays
// usable for a candle that opened before now and is removed after this bar.
killName(string n) =>
    if array.size(lvls) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(lvls) - 1
            Lvl lv = array.get(lvls, i)
            if lv.name == n and na(lv.deadT)
                lv.deadT := time
    true

// keep only the newest swKeep swing levels per side
trimSwings(int k) =>
    int cnt = 0
    if array.size(lvls) > 0
        for i = array.size(lvls) - 1 to 0
            Lvl lv = array.get(lvls, i)
            if lv.tier == 1 and lv.kind == k
                cnt += 1
                if cnt > swKeep
                    dropLvl(i)
    true

// R8 premium / discount: shorts above, longs below the midnight open, and the
// 18:00 open unless "Midnight open" is chosen. Before midnight the 18:00 open stands in.
pdOk(bool bull, float p) =>
    float mo = mOpenDay == koDay ? mOpen : na
    bool useE = pdMode != "Midnight open" or na(mo)
    bool have = not na(mo) or (useE and not na(koOpen))
    bool okM = na(mo) or (bull ? p < mo : p > mo)
    bool okE = not useE or na(koOpen) or (bull ? p < koOpen : p > koOpen)
    have and okM and okE

// R7: TP2 at a fixed R, the nearest untaken opposing liquidity, or the midnight open
tp2For(bool bull, float e, float rk) =>
    float res = bull ? e + tp2R * rk : e - tp2R * rk
    float t1  = bull ? e + tp1R * rk : e - tp1R * rk
    if tp2Mode == "Opposing liquidity" and array.size(lvls) > 0
        float best = na
        for i = 0 to array.size(lvls) - 1
            Lvl lv = array.get(lvls, i)
            if na(lv.takenT) and na(lv.deadT) and (bull ? lv.kind == 1 and lv.price > t1 : lv.kind == -1 and lv.price < t1)
                if na(best) or (bull ? lv.price < best : lv.price > best)
                    best := lv.price
        if not na(best)
            res := best
    else if tp2Mode == "Midnight open"
        float mo = mOpenDay == koDay ? mOpen : koOpen
        if not na(mo) and (bull ? mo > t1 : mo < t1)
            res := mo
    res

// R6
stopFor(bool bull, float e, float tip) =>
    fixStop ? (bull ? e - stopPts : e + stopPts) : (bull ? tip - stopTk * TICK : tip + stopTk * TICK)

mkTrade(bool bull, float e, float tip) =>
    float st = stopFor(bull, e, tip)
    float rk = math.abs(e - st)
    Trade.new(entry=e, stop=st, risk=rk, tp1=bull ? e + tp1R * rk : e - tp1R * rk, tp2=tp2For(bull, e, rk))

// A5: one bar of a resting limit. Returns true when it fills on this bar.
stepLimit(Trade t, bool bull, bool canFill, bool deadBefore, bool deadNow) =>
    bool filledNow = false
    if not t.filled and not t.cancelled
        if deadBefore
            t.cancelled := true
        else if canFill and (bull ? low <= t.entry : high >= t.entry)
            t.filled := true
            t.fillBar := bar_index
            filledNow := true
        else if deadNow or (bull ? high >= t.tp2 : low <= t.tp2)
            t.cancelled := true
    filledNow

// R5 CISD after tap. The first touch arms it; each new extreme resets the CISD
// level to the open of the run that made it; the entry is the first close back
// through that level. Returns true when it fills on this bar.
stepCisd(Trade t, RB r, bool canFill, bool deadBefore, bool deadNow, float cisdHere, bool flat) =>
    bool filledNow = false
    bool bull = r.bull
    if not t.filled and not t.cancelled
        if deadBefore
            t.cancelled := true
        else if not t.tapped
            if canFill and (bull ? low <= r.edge : high >= r.edge)
                t.tapped := true
                t.tapBar := bar_index
                t.ext := bull ? low : high
                t.extBar := bar_index
                t.cisd := cisdHere
            else if deadNow or (bull ? high >= r.t0.tp2 : low <= r.t0.tp2)
                t.cancelled := true
        else
            if bull ? low <= t.ext : high >= t.ext
                t.ext := bull ? low : high
                t.extBar := bar_index
                t.cisd := cisdHere
            else if not flat and not deadNow and not na(t.cisd) and bar_index > t.extBar and (bull ? close > t.cisd : close < t.cisd)
                float st = fixStop ? (bull ? close - stopPts : close + stopPts) : t.stop
                float rk = bull ? close - st : st - close
                if rk > 0
                    t.entry := close
                    t.stop := st
                    t.risk := rk
                    t.tp1 := bull ? close + tp1R * rk : close - tp1R * rk
                    t.tp2 := tp2For(bull, close, rk)
                    t.filled := true
                    t.fillBar := bar_index
                    filledNow := true
            if not t.filled and (deadNow or bar_index - t.tapBar >= cisdWin)
                t.cancelled := true
    filledNow

// A5: one bar of an open position. Stop first (conservative); targets from the
// bar after the fill. A limit can stop out on its fill bar; a CISD (market) entry
// is taken at the close, so its first bar is the next one.
stepOpen(Trade t, bool bull, bool mkt, bool flat) =>
    if t.filled and not (t.done1 and t.done2)
        bool after = bar_index > t.fillBar
        bool stopHit = (after or not mkt) and (bull ? low <= t.stop : high >= t.stop)
        if stopHit
            if not t.done1
                t.r1 := -1.0
                t.done1 := true
            if not t.done2
                t.r2 := -1.0
                t.done2 := true
        else if after
            if not t.done1 and (bull ? high >= t.tp1 : low <= t.tp1)
                t.r1 := math.abs(t.tp1 - t.entry) / t.risk
                t.done1 := true
            if not t.done2 and (bull ? high >= t.tp2 : low <= t.tp2)
                t.r2 := math.abs(t.tp2 - t.entry) / t.risk
                t.done2 := true
        if flat and not (t.done1 and t.done2)
            float rNow = (bull ? close - t.entry : t.entry - close) / t.risk
            if not t.done1
                t.r1 := rNow
                t.done1 := true
            if not t.done2
                t.r2 := rNow
                t.done2 := true
    true

// R8 entry factors at the fill, from what was known before this bar (A6)
entryFactors(RB r, Trade t) =>
    bool bull = r.bull
    float e = t.entry
    float wl = math.abs(r.edge - r.tip)
    bool el = false
    int np = bull ? array.size(pvL) : array.size(pvH)
    if np > 0
        for i = 0 to np - 1
            float p = bull ? array.get(pvL, i) : array.get(pvH, i)
            int   b = bull ? array.get(pvLB, i) : array.get(pvHB, i)
            if b >= r.trackFrom and (bull ? p > e and p <= r.edge + 0.25 * wl : p < e and p >= r.edge - 0.25 * wl)
                el := true
    bool lt = false
    int ng = array.size(lgTop)
    if ng > 0
        float tol = frontTk * TICK
        for i = 0 to ng - 1
            if array.get(lgBull, i) == bull and array.get(lgBar, i) < bar_index and e >= array.get(lgBot, i) - tol and e <= array.get(lgTop, i) + tol
                lt := true
    // the leg runs from the tip to the extreme made after the RB, beyond its own candle
    bool legOk = bull ? r.ext > r.far : r.ext < r.far
    float leg = bull ? r.ext - r.tip : r.tip - r.ext
    float rt  = legOk and leg > 0 ? (bull ? r.ext - e : e - r.ext) / leg : na
    bool ote = not na(rt) and rt >= oteLo and rt <= oteHi
    bool ny = false
    if not na(nyS) and not na(nyE)
        int m = nyMin(time)
        ny := nyS <= nyE ? m >= nyS and m < nyE : m >= nyS or m < nyE
    t.fEl   := el
    t.fLtf  := lt
    t.fOte  := ote
    t.fDisp := r.disp
    t.fNy   := ny
    t.score := r.sScore + (el ? 1 : 0) + (lt ? 1 : 0) + (ote ? 1 : 0) + (r.disp ? 1 : 0) + (ny ? 1 : 0)
    true

// ---- drawing ----
upLine(line ln, int x1, float y, color c) =>
    line res = ln
    if na(y)
        line.delete(ln)
        res := na
    else if na(ln)
        res := line.new(x1, y, bar_index, y, color=c, style=line.style_dashed, width=1)
    else
        line.set_xy1(ln, x1, y)
        line.set_xy2(ln, bar_index, y)
    res

upLab(label lb, float y, color c, string txt) =>
    label res = lb
    if na(y)
        label.delete(lb)
        res := na
    else if na(lb)
        res := label.new(bar_index, y, txt, color=color.new(color.black, 100), style=label.style_label_left, textcolor=c, size=size.tiny)
    else
        label.set_xy(lb, bar_index, y)
        label.set_text(lb, txt)
    res

clearTrade(RB r) =>
    line.delete(r.lnE)
    line.delete(r.lnS)
    line.delete(r.lnT1)
    line.delete(r.lnT2)
    label.delete(r.lbE)
    label.delete(r.lbS)
    label.delete(r.lbT1)
    label.delete(r.lbT2)
    r.lnE := na
    r.lnS := na
    r.lnT1 := na
    r.lnT2 := na
    r.lbE := na
    r.lbS := na
    r.lbT1 := na
    r.lbT2 := na
    true

// entry / stop / TP lines for the selected entry of a live RB
drawTrade(RB r) =>
    Trade t = trd(r, selIdx)
    bool waitC = selIdx == 3 and not t.filled
    float yE  = waitC ? r.edge : t.entry
    float yS  = waitC and fixStop ? na : t.stop
    float yT1 = waitC ? na : t.tp1
    float yT2 = waitC ? na : t.tp2
    string eTxt = waitC ? "Tap → wait for CISD" : (t.filled ? "Filled " : "Limit ") + array.get(ENTRY_NAMES, selIdx) + " " + px(yE)
    int x1 = math.max(r.formBar, bar_index - MAX_AGE)
    r.lnE := upLine(r.lnE, x1, yE, colEnt)
    r.lbE := upLab(r.lbE, yE, colEnt, eTxt)
    r.lnS := upLine(r.lnS, x1, yS, colSl)
    r.lbS := upLab(r.lbS, yS, colSl, "SL " + px(yS))
    r.lnT1 := upLine(r.lnT1, x1, yT1, colTp)
    r.lbT1 := upLab(r.lbT1, yT1, colTp, "TP1 " + px(yT1))
    r.lnT2 := upLine(r.lnT2, x1, yT2, colTp)
    r.lbT2 := upLab(r.lbT2, yT2, colTp, "TP2 " + px(yT2))
    true

deleteDrawings(RB r) =>
    box.delete(r.bx)
    line.delete(r.ceLn)
    line.delete(r.qLn)
    label.delete(r.tag)
    r.bx := na
    r.ceLn := na
    r.qLn := na
    r.tag := na
    clearTrade(r)
    true

setupText(RB r) =>
    "PD array " + yes(r.fPda) + " · Liquidity " + yes(r.fLiq) + " · P/D " + yes(r.fPd) + " · Bias " + yes(r.fBias) + " · Order flow " + yes(r.fOf) + " · Clean tip " + yes(r.fClean) + (smtOn ? " · SMT " + yes(r.fSmt) : "")

tagText(RB r) =>
    string t = (r.bull ? "▲ " : "▼ ") + str.tostring(r.sScore) + "/" + str.tostring(SETUPMAX) + (r.disp ? " ✓" : "")
    lblMode == "Full" ? t + " · " + r.names : t

tagTip(RB r) =>
    (r.bull ? "Bullish" : "Bearish") + " rejection block (" + rbName + ")\nRan: " + r.names + "\nGann  0 tip " + px(r.tip) + " · .25 " + px(r.q25) + " · .5 CE " + px(r.ce) + " · 1 edge " + px(r.edge) + "\nLimits  .5 @ " + px(r.t0.entry) + " · .25 @ " + px(r.t1.entry) + "   SL " + px(r.t0.stop) + "\nSetup " + str.tostring(r.sScore) + "/" + str.tostring(SETUPMAX) + ": " + setupText(r) + "\nDisplacement: " + (r.disp ? "printed (" + r.dispBy + ")" : "waiting, CISD at " + px(r.cisdLvl))

refreshTag(RB r) =>
    if not na(r.bx)
        box.set_border_style(r.bx, r.disp ? line.style_solid : line.style_dashed)
    if not na(r.tag)
        label.set_text(r.tag, tagText(r))
        label.set_tooltip(r.tag, tagTip(r))
    true

drawNewBox(RB r, color c) =>
    r.bx := box.new(left=r.formBar, top=math.max(r.tip, r.edge), right=bar_index, bottom=math.min(r.tip, r.edge), border_color=color.new(c, 30), border_style=r.disp ? line.style_solid : line.style_dashed, bgcolor=color.new(c, 85))
    if showGann
        r.ceLn := line.new(r.formBar, r.ce, bar_index, r.ce, color=color.new(c, 10), style=line.style_dotted, width=1)
        r.qLn  := line.new(r.formBar, r.q25, bar_index, r.q25, color=color.new(c, 55), style=line.style_dotted, width=1)
    if lblMode != "Off"
        r.tag := label.new(r.formBar, r.tip, tagText(r), color=color.new(color.black, 100), style=r.bull ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, textcolor=c, size=size.tiny, tooltip=tagTip(r))
    true

drawNew(RB r) =>
    color c = r.bull ? colBull : colBear
    if clean
        r.bx := na
        r.tag := na
    else
        drawNewBox(r, c)
    true

// the zone has stopped being live: freeze and dim its drawings
endZone(RB r) =>
    r.zoneDone := true
    color c = r.bull ? colBull : colBear
    if not keepLbl
        label.delete(r.tag)
        r.tag := na
    if not na(r.bx)
        box.set_right(r.bx, bar_index)
        box.set_bgcolor(r.bx, color.new(c, 94))
        box.set_border_color(r.bx, color.new(c, 70))
    if not na(r.ceLn)
        line.set_x2(r.ceLn, bar_index)
        line.set_color(r.ceLn, color.new(c, 70))
    if not na(r.qLn)
        line.set_x2(r.qLn, bar_index)
        line.set_color(r.qLn, color.new(c, 85))
    true

sizeTxt(float s) =>
    s >= 1 ? "×1" : s >= 0.5 ? "×½" : s >= 0.25 ? "×¼" : "×" + str.tostring(s, "0.###")

markTip(RB r, Trade t) =>
    (r.bull ? "Bottom tick · long @ " : "Top tick · short @ ") + px(t.entry) + " (" + array.get(ENTRY_NAMES, selIdx) + ")\nGrade " + gradeOf(t.score, MAXS) + " · score " + str.tostring(t.score) + "/" + str.tostring(MAXS) + "\nSL " + px(t.stop) + "  TP1 " + px(t.tp1) + "  TP2 " + px(t.tp2) + "\nRB " + rbName + " off " + r.names + "\nSetup: " + setupText(r) + "\nEntry: Engineered liquidity " + yes(t.fEl) + " · LTF gap " + yes(t.fLtf) + " · OTE " + yes(t.fOte) + " · Displaced " + yes(t.fDisp) + " · Session " + yes(t.fNy) + (t.size > 0 ? "\nDaily plan trade, size " + sizeTxt(t.size) : "")

// Clean style: an arrow on the wick that was traded, and a TradingView-style
// position box from the wick to the exit: green to the target, red to the stop
addArrowBox(RB r, Trade t) =>
    float tgt = planTgt == "TP1" ? t.tp1 : t.tp2
    label a = label.new(math.max(r.tipBar, bar_index - MAX_AGE), r.tip, "", style=r.bull ? label.style_arrowup : label.style_arrowdown, color=r.bull ? colBotA : colTopA, size=size.normal, tooltip=markTip(r, t))
    array.push(marks, a)
    // the box starts at the wick (the limit rests from there); the dot marks the fill
    int x0 = math.max(r.tipBar, bar_index - MAX_AGE)
    array.push(marks, label.new(bar_index, t.entry, "", style=label.style_circle, color=#787b86, size=size.tiny, tooltip="Filled here"))
    t.pW := box.new(x0, math.max(t.entry, tgt), bar_index + 1, math.min(t.entry, tgt), border_color=color.new(#089981, 40), bgcolor=color.new(#089981, 78))
    t.pL := box.new(x0, math.max(t.entry, t.stop), bar_index + 1, math.min(t.entry, t.stop), border_color=color.new(#f23645, 40), bgcolor=color.new(#f23645, 78))
    t.lbT := label.new(bar_index + 1, tgt, px(tgt), style=label.style_label_left, color=#089981, textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
    t.lbE := label.new(bar_index + 1, t.entry, px(t.entry), style=label.style_label_left, color=#787b86, textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
    t.lbS := label.new(bar_index + 1, t.stop, px(t.stop), style=label.style_label_left, color=#f23645, textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
    array.push(boxedT, t)
    if array.size(marks) > markKeep
        label.delete(array.shift(marks))
    if array.size(boxedT) > markKeep
        Trade o = array.shift(boxedT)
        box.delete(o.pW)
        box.delete(o.pL)
        label.delete(o.lbT)
        label.delete(o.lbE)
        label.delete(o.lbS)
    true

// Detailed style: a TOP / BOT label at the fill price
addLabelMark(RB r, Trade t) =>
    color c = r.bull ? colBull : colBear
    string txt = (r.bull ? "BOT " : "TOP ") + gradeOf(t.score, MAXS) + (t.size > 0 ? " " + sizeTxt(t.size) : "")
    label lb = label.new(bar_index, t.entry, txt, color=color.new(c, 10), style=r.bull ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, textcolor=color.white, size=size.small, tooltip=markTip(r, t))
    array.push(marks, lb)
    if array.size(marks) > markKeep
        label.delete(array.shift(marks))
    true

// TOP / BOT marker where the selected entry filled
addMark(RB r, Trade t) =>
    if clean
        addArrowBox(r, t)
    else
        addLabelMark(r, t)
    true

// A7: add a resolved RB to the stats
countRB(RB r) =>
    for m = 0 to 3
        Trade t = trd(r, m)
        if t.filled and passes(t)
            array.set(eFill, m, array.get(eFill, m) + 1)
            array.set(eS1, m, array.get(eS1, m) + t.r1)
            array.set(eW1, m, array.get(eW1, m) + (t.r1 > 0 ? 1 : 0))
            array.set(eS2, m, array.get(eS2, m) + t.r2)
            array.set(eW2, m, array.get(eW2, m) + (t.r2 > 0 ? 1 : 0))
    Trade ts = trd(r, selIdx)
    if ts.filled
        string g = gradeOf(ts.score, MAXS)
        for k = 0 to LAB_N - 1
            bool inRow = switch k
                0  => true
                1  => r.fPda
                2  => r.fLiq
                3  => r.fPd
                4  => r.fBias
                5  => r.fOf
                6  => r.fClean
                7  => r.fSmt
                8  => ts.fEl
                9  => ts.fLtf
                10 => ts.fOte
                11 => ts.fDisp
                12 => ts.fNy
                13 => g == "A+"
                14 => g == "A"
                15 => g == "B"
                => g == "C"
            if inRow
                array.set(lN, k, array.get(lN, k) + 1)
                array.set(lS1, k, array.get(lS1, k) + ts.r1)
                array.set(lW1, k, array.get(lW1, k) + (ts.r1 > 0 ? 1 : 0))
                array.set(lS2, k, array.get(lS2, k) + ts.r2)
                array.set(lW2, k, array.get(lW2, k) + (ts.r2 > 0 ? 1 : 0))
    true

// ---- HTF gaps (R2) ----
addGap(bool bull, float top, float bot, string nm, int bt, int left) =>
    int lft = math.max(left, bar_index - MAX_AGE)
    Gap g = Gap.new(bull=bull, top=top, bot=bot, name=nm, bornT=bt, left=lft)
    if showFvg
        g.bx := box.new(left=lft, top=top, right=bar_index, bottom=bot, border_color=color.new(colFvg, 55), bgcolor=color.new(colFvg, 88), text=nm, text_size=size.tiny, text_color=color.new(colFvg, 20), text_halign=text.align_right, text_valign=bull ? text.align_bottom : text.align_top)
    array.push(gaps, g)
    // keep the newest fvgKeep per timeframe and side
    int cnt = 0
    for i = array.size(gaps) - 1 to 0
        Gap q = array.get(gaps, i)
        if q.name == nm and q.bull == bull
            cnt += 1
            if cnt > fvgKeep
                box.delete(q.bx)
                array.remove(gaps, i)
    true

// One closed gap-timeframe candle: fair value gaps (R2), order flow from its
// 3-candle swings (A8), and its high/low as liquidity (R3).
pdaClose(Agg a, string nm, bool late, bool isOf) =>
    array.push(a.H, a.h)
    array.push(a.L, a.l)
    array.push(a.B, a.bar)
    if array.size(a.H) > 5
        array.shift(a.H)
        array.shift(a.L)
        array.shift(a.B)
    int n = array.size(a.H)
    int bt = late ? time : time_close
    if isOf
        if not na(S.swH) and a.c > S.swH
            S.ofDir := 1
            S.swH := na
        if not na(S.swL) and a.c < S.swL
            S.ofDir := -1
            S.swL := na
    if n >= 3
        float h1 = array.get(a.H, n - 3)
        float l1 = array.get(a.L, n - 3)
        float h2 = array.get(a.H, n - 2)
        float l2 = array.get(a.L, n - 2)
        float h3 = array.get(a.H, n - 1)
        float l3 = array.get(a.L, n - 1)
        int left = array.get(a.B, n - 3)
        if l3 - h1 >= fvgMinTk * TICK
            addGap(true, l3, h1, nm + " FVG", bt, left)
        if l1 - h3 >= fvgMinTk * TICK
            addGap(false, l1, h3, nm + " FVG", bt, left)
        if isOf
            if h2 > h1 and h2 > h3
                S.swH := h2
            if l2 < l1 and l2 < l3
                S.swL := l2
    if useHtfC
        killName(nm + " H")
        killName(nm + " L")
        addLvl(a.h, nm + " H", 1, 2, bt, koDay)
        addLvl(a.l, nm + " L", -1, 2, bt, koDay)
    true

// build a gap-timeframe candle from chart bars; finalize it on its last bar (A1)
pdaStep(Agg a, string nm, bool newBar, bool lastBar, bool isOf) =>
    if newBar
        if not a.done and not na(a.o)
            pdaClose(a, nm, true, isOf)
        a.o := open
        a.h := high
        a.l := low
        a.c := close
        a.bar := bar_index
        a.done := false
    else if not na(a.o)
        a.h := math.max(a.h, high)
        a.l := math.min(a.l, low)
        a.c := close
    if lastBar and not a.done and not na(a.o)
        pdaClose(a, nm, false, isOf)
        a.done := true
    true

// Finalize one closed RB-timeframe candle: age and displacement for live RBs,
// then look for a new RB (R1-R4) against the gaps and levels as they stood
// before it (A2), then store the candle, confirm swings, drop spent liquidity.
// late = finalized on the first bar of the next candle (A1). sh/sl = SMT symbol.
finalize(float o, float h, float l, float c, int cT, int b0, bool late, float sh, float sl, int hb, int lb) =>
    if array.size(rbs) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(rbs) - 1
            RB r = array.get(rbs, i)
            if not r.resolved and not r.zoneDone and r.formT < cT
                r.age := r.age + 1
                if not r.disp and r.dispCount < dispWin
                    r.dispCount := r.dispCount + 1
                    if r.bull ? c > r.cisdLvl : c < r.cisdLvl
                        r.disp := true
                        r.dispBy := "CISD"
                        refreshTag(r)

    float bodyTop = math.max(o, c)
    float bodyBot = math.min(o, c)
    float rng  = h - l
    float upW  = h - bodyTop
    float dnW  = bodyBot - l
    float body = bodyTop - bodyBot
    float atrV = S.atr
    bool capUp = maxWickAtr <= 0 or na(atrV) or upW <= maxWickAtr * atrV
    bool capDn = maxWickAtr <= 0 or na(atrV) or dnW <= maxWickAtr * atrV
    bool bearShape = rng > 0 and upW >= minWickPct / 100.0 * rng and upW >= minWickBody * body and upW > dnW and (na(atrV) or minWickAtr <= 0 or upW >= minWickAtr * atrV) and capUp
    bool bullShape = rng > 0 and dnW >= minWickPct / 100.0 * rng and dnW >= minWickBody * body and dnW > upW and (na(atrV) or minWickAtr <= 0 or dnW >= minWickAtr * atrV) and capDn
    int nh = array.size(hH)
    RB rbNew = na
    if bearShape or bullShape
        bool bull = bullShape
        array<string> nmG = array.new<string>()
        array<string> nm3 = array.new<string>()
        array<string> nm2 = array.new<string>()
        array<string> nm1 = array.new<string>()
        array<string> nm0 = array.new<string>()
        bool hitG = false
        int bestTier = -1
        // R2: the wick reaches an HTF gap and the body stays on this side of its far edge
        if array.size(gaps) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(gaps) - 1
                Gap g = array.get(gaps, i)
                if g.bull == bull and g.bornT <= cT and (na(g.invT) or g.invT >= cT)
                    if bull ? l <= g.top and bodyBot > g.bot : h >= g.bot and bodyTop < g.top
                        hitG := true
                        if not array.includes(nmG, g.name)
                            array.push(nmG, g.name)
        // R3: liquidity and key opens
        if array.size(lvls) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(lvls) - 1
                Lvl lv = array.get(lvls, i)
                if lv.bornT <= cT and (na(lv.deadT) or cT < lv.deadT)
                    bool untaken = na(lv.takenT) or lv.takenT >= cT
                    bool hit = false
                    if lv.kind == 0
                        hit := bull ? l <= lv.price and bodyBot > lv.price : h >= lv.price and bodyTop < lv.price
                    else if bull and lv.kind == -1 and untaken
                        hit := l <= lv.price - sweepTk * TICK and bodyBot > lv.price
                    else if not bull and lv.kind == 1 and untaken
                        hit := h >= lv.price + sweepTk * TICK and bodyTop < lv.price
                    if hit
                        array.push(lv.tier == 3 ? nm3 : lv.tier == 2 ? nm2 : nm1, lv.name)
                        bestTier := math.max(bestTier, lv.tier)
        // R3: the previous RB candle (Shinobi), the weakest trigger
        if usePrev and nh > 0
            float ph = array.get(hH, nh - 1)
            float pl = array.get(hL, nh - 1)
            if bull ? l <= pl - sweepTk * TICK and bodyBot > pl : h >= ph + sweepTk * TICK and bodyTop < ph
                array.push(nm0, bull ? "Prev L" : "Prev H")
                bestTier := math.max(bestTier, 0)
        if hitG or bestTier >= 0
            // label names, gaps and key levels first, at most three
            array<string> nmAll = array.concat(array.concat(array.concat(array.concat(nmG, nm3), nm2), nm1), nm0)
            string names = array.join(array.slice(nmAll, 0, math.min(3, array.size(nmAll))), "+") + (array.size(nmAll) > 3 ? "+" + str.tostring(array.size(nmAll) - 3) : "")
            // R4: Gann box on the wick
            float tip  = bull ? l : h
            float edge = zoneFrom == "Close" ? c : bull ? bodyBot : bodyTop
            float ce   = (tip + edge) / 2
            float q25  = tip + 0.25 * (edge - tip)
            // A4: a wick inside a live RB of the same direction is a retest of it
            bool dup = false
            if array.size(rbs) > 0
                for i = 0 to array.size(rbs) - 1
                    RB q = array.get(rbs, i)
                    if q.bull == bull and not q.zoneDone and not q.resolved
                        if bull ? tip >= q.tip and tip <= q.edge : tip <= q.tip and tip >= q.edge
                            dup := true
            // R8 setup factors
            bool fPda  = hitG
            bool fLiq  = bestTier >= 1
            bool fPd   = pdOk(bull, ce)
            bool fBias = bias == (bull ? 1 : -1)
            bool fOf   = S.ofDir == (bull ? 1 : -1)
            bool fClean = true
            if nh > 0
                for j = math.max(0, nh - eqLook) to nh - 1
                    float x = bull ? array.get(hL, j) : array.get(hH, j)
                    if math.abs(x - tip) <= eqTk * TICK
                        fClean := false
            bool fSmt = false
            if smtOn and nh > 0 and not na(sh) and not na(sl)
                float mxH = na
                float mnL = na
                float sxH = na
                float snL = na
                for j = math.max(0, nh - smtLook) to nh - 1
                    mxH := na(mxH) ? array.get(hH, j) : math.max(mxH, array.get(hH, j))
                    mnL := na(mnL) ? array.get(hL, j) : math.min(mnL, array.get(hL, j))
                    float a1 = array.get(hSH, j)
                    float a2 = array.get(hSL, j)
                    if not na(a1)
                        sxH := na(sxH) ? a1 : math.max(sxH, a1)
                    if not na(a2)
                        snL := na(snL) ? a2 : math.min(snL, a2)
                fSmt := bull ? not na(snL) and l < mnL and sl >= snL : not na(sxH) and h > mxH and sh <= sxH
            int sc = (fPda ? 1 : 0) + (fLiq ? 1 : 0) + (fPd ? 1 : 0) + (fBias ? 1 : 0) + (fOf ? 1 : 0) + (fClean ? 1 : 0) + (fSmt ? 1 : 0)
            float fr  = frontTk * TICK
            float eCE = bull ? math.min(ce + fr, edge) : math.max(ce - fr, edge)
            float eQ  = bull ? math.min(q25 + fr, edge) : math.max(q25 - fr, edge)
            bool tooWide = maxStop > 0 and math.abs(eCE - stopFor(bull, eCE, tip)) > maxStop
            bool isExt = true
            if swingN > 0 and nh > 0
                for j = math.max(0, nh - swingN) to nh - 1
                    if bull ? array.get(hL, j) < l : array.get(hH, j) > h
                        isExt := false
            bool show = isExt and not flatNow and not dup and not tooWide and sc >= minSetup and (not reqPda or fPda) and (not reqLiq or fLiq) and (not reqPd or fPd) and (not reqBias or fBias) and (not reqOf or fOf) and (not reqClean or fClean)
            // CISD level = open of the run of candles that pushed into the sweep
            float runOpen = na
            int   runBar  = b0
            if bull ? c < o : c > o
                runOpen := o
            int jj = nh - 1
            int steps = 0
            while jj >= 0 and steps < 10
                float oj = array.get(hO, jj)
                float cj = array.get(hC, jj)
                if bull ? cj < oj : cj > oj
                    runOpen := oj
                    runBar := array.get(hB, jj)
                    jj -= 1
                    steps += 1
                else
                    break
            float cisdLvl = na(runOpen) ? (bull ? h : l) : runOpen
            bool dispNow = bull ? c > cisdLvl : c < cisdLvl
            // A1: a late candle is dropped if this bar already took its tip
            bool tapNow = false
            if show and late
                bool invNow = invWick ? (bull ? low < tip : high > tip) : (bull ? close < tip : close > tip)
                tapNow := bull ? low <= edge : high >= edge
                if invNow
                    show := false
            if show
                Trade tA = mkTrade(bull, eCE, tip)
                Trade tQ = mkTrade(bull, eQ, tip)
                Trade tE = mkTrade(bull, edge, tip)
                Trade tC = Trade.new(stop=stopFor(bull, edge, tip))
                rbNew := RB.new(bull=bull, tip=tip, edge=edge, ce=ce, q25=q25, names=names, formT=cT, formBar=b0, tipBar=bull ? lb : hb, legBar=runBar, trackFrom=bar_index + 1, fillFrom=bar_index + 1, cisdLvl=cisdLvl, disp=dispNow, dispBy=dispNow ? "CISD" : "", tapped=tapNow, far=bull ? h : l, ext=bull ? h : l, sScore=sc, fPda=fPda, fLiq=fLiq, fPd=fPd, fBias=fBias, fOf=fOf, fClean=fClean, fSmt=fSmt, t0=tA, t1=tQ, t2=tE, t3=tC)

    // store the candle and update ATR(14) of the RB timeframe
    float prevC = nh > 0 ? array.get(hC, nh - 1) : na
    float tr = na(prevC) ? h - l : math.max(h, prevC) - math.min(l, prevC)
    S.atr := na(S.atr) ? tr : S.atr + (tr - S.atr) / 14.0
    array.push(hO, o)
    array.push(hH, h)
    array.push(hL, l)
    array.push(hC, c)
    array.push(hB, b0)
    array.push(hSH, sh)
    array.push(hSL, sl)
    if array.size(hO) > 60
        array.shift(hO)
        array.shift(hH)
        array.shift(hL)
        array.shift(hC)
        array.shift(hB)
        array.shift(hSH)
        array.shift(hSL)

    // swing points confirmed by this candle (live from its close, A2)
    if useSw
        int ns = array.size(hH)
        if ns >= 2 * swLen + 1
            int cI = ns - 1 - swLen
            float sph = array.get(hH, cI)
            float spl = array.get(hL, cI)
            bool isPH = true
            bool isPL = true
            for k = cI - swLen to cI + swLen
                if k != cI
                    if array.get(hH, k) >= sph
                        isPH := false
                    if array.get(hL, k) <= spl
                        isPL := false
            int bt = late ? time : time_close
            if isPH
                addLvl(sph, "Swing H", 1, 1, bt, koDay)
                trimSwings(1)
            if isPL
                addLvl(spl, "Swing L", -1, 1, bt, koDay)
                trimSwings(-1)

    // one-sided liquidity traded through by this candle (or before it) is spent
    if array.size(lvls) > 0
        for i = array.size(lvls) - 1 to 0
            Lvl lv = array.get(lvls, i)
            if lv.kind != 0 and not na(lv.takenT) and (not late or lv.takenT < time)
                dropLvl(i)
    rbNew

// ============================== ENGINE =======================================
bool aNewBull = false
bool aNewBear = false
bool aTop     = false
bool aBot     = false
bool aInval   = false

if barstate.isconfirmed
    // ---- chart-bar runs for the CISD trigger (R5)
    float prevUp = upRun
    float prevDn = dnRun
    if close > open
        upRun := na(upRun) ? open : upRun
        dnRun := na
    else if close < open
        dnRun := na(dnRun) ? open : dnRun
        upRun := na
    else
        upRun := na
        dnRun := na
    float cisdBear = close > open ? upRun : na(prevUp) ? open : prevUp
    float cisdBull = close < open ? dnRun : na(prevDn) ? open : prevDn

    // ---- day / week levels and the PXH/PXL daily bias (R3, A8)
    if newDay
        if not na(dO)
            float dC = close[1]
            if not na(pdH)
                bool tookH = dH > pdH
                bool tookL = dL < pdL
                bias := dC > pdH ? 1 : dC < pdL ? -1 : tookH and not tookL ? -1 : tookL and not tookH ? 1 : dC >= dO ? 1 : -1
            else
                bias := dC >= dO ? 1 : -1
            pdH := dH
            pdL := dL
            if usePD
                killName("PDH")
                killName("PDL")
                addLvl(dH, "PDH", 1, 3, time, koDay)
                addLvl(dL, "PDL", -1, 3, time, koDay)
        dO := open
        dH := high
        dL := low
    else
        if na(dO)
            dO := open
        dH := na(dH) ? high : math.max(dH, high)
        dL := na(dL) ? low : math.min(dL, low)
    if newWeek
        if usePW and not na(wH)
            killName("PWH")
            killName("PWL")
            addLvl(wH, "PWH", 1, 3, time, koDay)
            addLvl(wL, "PWL", -1, 3, time, koDay)
        wH := high
        wL := low
    else
        wH := na(wH) ? high : math.max(wH, high)
        wL := na(wL) ? low : math.min(wL, low)
    if mNow >= 1080
        sawEve := true
    if sawEve ? cross18 : newDay
        koDay += 1
        koOpen := open
    if newNyDate
        mOpen := open
        mOpenDay := koDay
    if useKO
        string koName = mNow == 1080 and ko1800 ? "18:00" : mNow == 0 and ko0000 ? "00:00" : mNow == 120 and ko0200 ? "02:00" : mNow == 510 and ko0830 ? "08:30" : mNow == 570 and ko0930 ? "09:30" : mNow == 600 and ko1000 ? "10:00" : mNow == 780 and ko1300 ? "13:00" : mNow == 810 and ko1330 ? "13:30" : ""
        if koName != ""
            addLvl(open, koName, 0, 2, time + 1, koDay)
    if useSes
        bool nAs = mNow >= 1200
        bool nLn = mNow >= 120 and mNow < 300
        bool nNy = mNow >= 570 and mNow < 720
        if nAs
            asH := inAs ? math.max(asH, high) : high
            asL := inAs ? math.min(asL, low) : low
        else if inAs
            killName("Asia H")
            killName("Asia L")
            addLvl(asH, "Asia H", 1, 2, time, koDay)
            addLvl(asL, "Asia L", -1, 2, time, koDay)
        if nLn
            lnH := inLn ? math.max(lnH, high) : high
            lnL := inLn ? math.min(lnL, low) : low
        else if inLn
            killName("London H")
            killName("London L")
            addLvl(lnH, "London H", 1, 2, time, koDay)
            addLvl(lnL, "London L", -1, 2, time, koDay)
        if nNy
            nyH := inNy ? math.max(nyH, high) : high
            nyL := inNy ? math.min(nyL, low) : low
        else if inNy
            killName("NY AM H")
            killName("NY AM L")
            addLvl(nyH, "NY AM H", 1, 2, time, koDay)
            addLvl(nyL, "NY AM L", -1, 2, time, koDay)
        inAs := nAs
        inLn := nLn
        inNy := nNy

    // ---- daily plan: a new trading day starts once no plan trade is open (A9)
    if planDay != koDay and na(planT)
        if dayTrades > 0
            planDays += 1
            planWinD += dayR > 0 ? 1 : 0
        planDay := koDay
        dayTrades := 0
        dayDone := false
        dayR := 0.0

    // ---- one-sided liquidity traded through on this bar (A2)
    if array.size(lvls) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(lvls) - 1
            Lvl lv = array.get(lvls, i)
            if lv.kind != 0 and na(lv.takenT) and time >= lv.bornT
                if lv.kind == 1 ? high >= lv.price + sweepTk * TICK : low <= lv.price - sweepTk * TICK
                    lv.takenT := time

    // ---- HTF gaps closed through on this bar die (R2)
    if array.size(gaps) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(gaps) - 1
            Gap g = array.get(gaps, i)
            if na(g.invT) and time >= g.bornT and (g.bull ? close < g.bot : close > g.top)
                g.invT := time
                box.delete(g.bx)
                g.bx := na

    // ---- track every RB already on the chart through this bar (R5, R6, A5)
    if array.size(rbs) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(rbs) - 1
            RB r = array.get(rbs, i)
            if not r.resolved and bar_index >= r.trackFrom
                bool deadBefore = r.zoneDone
                if not deadBefore and rbLife > 0 and r.age >= rbLife
                    r.expired := true
                    endZone(r)
                    deadBefore := true
                bool deadNow = false
                if not deadBefore
                    if not r.tapped and (r.bull ? low <= r.edge : high >= r.edge)
                        r.tapped := true
                    bool inv = invWick ? (r.bull ? low < r.tip : high > r.tip) : (r.bull ? close < r.tip : close > r.tip)
                    if inv
                        r.invalid := true
                        deadNow := true
                        Trade tsI = trd(r, selIdx)
                        if not tsI.filled and not tsI.cancelled
                            aInval := true
                            alert((r.bull ? "Bullish" : "Bearish") + " RB invalidated before entry (tip " + px(r.tip) + " taken) · " + syminfo.ticker, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
                    if flatNow or bar_index - r.formBar > MAX_AGE
                        r.expired := true
                        deadNow := true
                bool canFill = bar_index >= r.fillFrom
                for m = 0 to 3
                    Trade t = trd(r, m)
                    bool fNow = m == 3 ? stepCisd(t, r, canFill, deadBefore, deadNow, r.bull ? cisdBull : cisdBear, flatNow) : stepLimit(t, r.bull, canFill, deadBefore, deadNow)
                    if fNow
                        entryFactors(r, t)
                        bool planOk = planOn and planDay == koDay and not dayDone and na(planT) and dayTrades < planMax
                        if m == selIdx and passes(t) and (not reqSess or t.fNy) and (planOk or not planOn)
                            if planOk
                                t.size := math.pow(0.5, dayTrades)
                                planT := t
                                dayTrades += 1
                            addMark(r, t)
                            if r.bull
                                aBot := true
                            else
                                aTop := true
                            alert((r.bull ? "BOTTOM TICK · long " : "TOP TICK · short ") + syminfo.ticker + " @ " + px(t.entry) + " (" + array.get(ENTRY_NAMES, m) + ") · grade " + gradeOf(t.score, MAXS) + " " + str.tostring(t.score) + "/" + str.tostring(MAXS) + " · SL " + px(t.stop) + " · TP1 " + px(t.tp1) + " · TP2 " + px(t.tp2) + (t.size > 0 ? " · plan size " + sizeTxt(t.size) : ""), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
                    stepOpen(t, r.bull, m == 3, flatNow)
                if deadNow and not r.zoneDone
                    endZone(r)
                if isDone(r.t0) and isDone(r.t1) and isDone(r.t2) and isDone(r.t3)
                    r.resolved := true
                    if not r.zoneDone
                        endZone(r)
                    countRB(r)
                    setups += 1
                else if not r.zoneDone
                    if not na(r.bx)
                        box.set_right(r.bx, bar_index)
                    if not na(r.ceLn)
                        line.set_x2(r.ceLn, bar_index)
                    if not na(r.qLn)
                        line.set_x2(r.qLn, bar_index)
                // the leg off the tip, through this bar, for OTE from the next bar (A6)
                r.ext := r.bull ? math.max(r.ext, high) : math.min(r.ext, low)

    // ---- the open plan trade resolves at its plan target (R9)
    if not na(planT)
        if planTgt == "TP1" ? planT.done1 : planT.done2
            float rr = (planTgt == "TP1" ? planT.r1 : planT.r2) * planT.size
            dayR += rr
            planR += rr
            planN += 1
            planW += rr > 0 ? 1 : 0
            if rr > 0 or dayTrades >= planMax
                dayDone := true
            planT := na

    // ---- position boxes run until their trade exits, then show the result
    if array.size(boxedT) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(boxedT) - 1
            Trade t = array.get(boxedT, i)
            if not t.boxDone
                bool fin = planTgt == "TP1" ? t.done1 : t.done2
                int x2 = math.max(bar_index, t.fillBar + 1)
                box.set_right(t.pW, x2)
                box.set_right(t.pL, x2)
                label.set_x(t.lbT, x2)
                label.set_x(t.lbE, x2)
                label.set_x(t.lbS, x2)
                if fin
                    t.boxDone := true
                    float rr = planTgt == "TP1" ? t.r1 : t.r2
                    label.set_text(t.lbE, fRs(rr))
                    label.set_color(t.lbE, rr > 0 ? #089981 : #f23645)

    // ---- chart-timeframe gaps. Closing through one from the leg into a live RB's
    // tip displaces that RB (GS: inverse the gaps in the leg); live ones are entry factors.
    if array.size(lgTop) > 0
        for i = array.size(lgTop) - 1 to 0
            bool gb = array.get(lgBull, i)
            if gb ? close < array.get(lgBot, i) : close > array.get(lgTop, i)
                int gm = array.get(lgBar, i) - 1
                if array.size(rbs) > 0
                    for k = 0 to array.size(rbs) - 1
                        RB r = array.get(rbs, k)
                        if r.bull != gb and not r.resolved and not r.zoneDone and not r.disp and bar_index >= r.trackFrom and gm >= r.legBar and gm < r.trackFrom
                            r.disp := true
                            r.dispBy := "IFVG"
                            refreshTag(r)
                array.remove(lgBull, i)
                array.remove(lgTop, i)
                array.remove(lgBot, i)
                array.remove(lgBar, i)
    if low > high[2] and low - high[2] >= ltfMinTk * TICK
        array.push(lgBull, true)
        array.push(lgTop, low)
        array.push(lgBot, high[2])
        array.push(lgBar, bar_index)
    if high < low[2] and low[2] - high >= ltfMinTk * TICK
        array.push(lgBull, false)
        array.push(lgTop, low[2])
        array.push(lgBot, high)
        array.push(lgBar, bar_index)
    while array.size(lgTop) > 40
        array.shift(lgBull)
        array.shift(lgTop)
        array.shift(lgBot)
        array.shift(lgBar)

    // ---- chart-timeframe swings confirmed on this bar (engineered liquidity, A6)
    if not na(pvhNow)
        array.push(pvH, pvhNow)
        array.push(pvHB, bar_index - elStr)
        if array.size(pvH) > 30
            array.shift(pvH)
            array.shift(pvHB)
    if not na(pvlNow)
        array.push(pvL, pvlNow)
        array.push(pvLB, bar_index - elStr)
        if array.size(pvL) > 30
            array.shift(pvL)
            array.shift(pvLB)

    // ---- gap-timeframe candles (R2, A8)
    if onA
        pdaStep(AA, nameA, newABar, lastABar, true)
    if onB
        pdaStep(AB, nameB, newBBar, lastBBar, not onA)

    // ---- build the RB-timeframe candle; finalize it on its last bar (A1)
    RB made1 = na
    RB made2 = na
    if newRbBar
        if not aDone and not na(aO)
            made1 := finalize(aO, aH, aL, aC, aT, aBar, true, aSH, aSL, aHB, aLB)
        aO    := open
        aH    := high
        aL    := low
        aC    := close
        aSH   := smtH
        aSL   := smtL
        aT    := time
        aBar  := bar_index
        aHB   := bar_index
        aLB   := bar_index
        aDone := false
    else if not na(aO)
        if high > aH
            aHB := bar_index
        if low < aL
            aLB := bar_index
        aH  := math.max(aH, high)
        aL  := math.min(aL, low)
        aC  := close
        aSH := na(smtH) ? aSH : na(aSH) ? smtH : math.max(aSH, smtH)
        aSL := na(smtL) ? aSL : na(aSL) ? smtL : math.min(aSL, smtL)
    if lastRbBar and not aDone and not na(aO)
        made2 := finalize(aO, aH, aL, aC, aT, aBar, false, aSH, aSL, aHB, aLB)
        aDone := true

    for k = 0 to 1
        RB nr = k == 0 ? made1 : made2
        if not na(nr)
            drawNew(nr)
            array.push(rbs, nr)
            if nr.bull
                aNewBull := true
            else
                aNewBear := true
            Trade tn = trd(nr, selIdx)
            alert((nr.bull ? "Bullish" : "Bearish") + " RB " + rbName + " [setup " + str.tostring(nr.sScore) + "/" + str.tostring(SETUPMAX) + "] off " + nr.names + " · " + (selIdx == 3 ? "wait for a tap, then CISD" : "limit " + array.get(ENTRY_NAMES, selIdx) + " @ " + px(tn.entry) + " · SL " + px(tn.stop)) + " · " + syminfo.ticker, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

    // ---- gaps that died before the current RB candle opened go; live ones extend
    if array.size(gaps) > 0
        for i = array.size(gaps) - 1 to 0
            Gap g = array.get(gaps, i)
            if not na(g.invT) and g.invT < aT
                array.remove(gaps, i)
            else if not na(g.bx)
                if bar_index - g.left > MAX_AGE
                    g.left := bar_index - MAX_AGE
                    box.set_left(g.bx, g.left)
                box.set_right(g.bx, bar_index)

    // ---- replaced levels go, and yesterday's key opens expire (A3)
    if array.size(lvls) > 0
        for i = array.size(lvls) - 1 to 0
            Lvl lv = array.get(lvls, i)
            if not na(lv.deadT) or (lv.kind == 0 and lv.dayId < koDay)
                dropLvl(i)

    // ---- extend level lines
    if array.size(lvls) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(lvls) - 1
            Lvl lv = array.get(lvls, i)
            if not na(lv.ln)
                if bar_index - lv.bornBar > MAX_AGE
                    line.set_x1(lv.ln, bar_index - MAX_AGE)
                line.set_x2(lv.ln, bar_index)

    // ---- entry / stop / TP lines for the newest live RBs; only the newest maxKeep
    // RBs that are still drawn keep their drawings, and finished RBs with none are dropped
    int liveShown = 0
    int kept = 0
    int total = 0
    if array.size(rbs) > 0
        for i = array.size(rbs) - 1 to 0
            RB r = array.get(rbs, i)
            bool active = not r.resolved and not na(r.bx) and not isDone(trd(r, selIdx))
            if active and liveShown < lvlN
                liveShown += 1
                drawTrade(r)
            else
                clearTrade(r)
            if not na(r.bx)
                kept += 1
                if kept > maxKeep
                    deleteDrawings(r)
            total += 1
            if na(r.bx) and (r.resolved or total > 300)
                array.remove(rbs, i)

// ============================== ALERTS =======================================
alertcondition(aNewBull, "Bullish RB formed", "Bullish rejection block formed: limit resting")
alertcondition(aNewBear, "Bearish RB formed", "Bearish rejection block formed: limit resting")
alertcondition(aBot, "BOTTOM tick (long fill)", "Bottom tick: rejection block long filled")
alertcondition(aTop, "TOP tick (short fill)", "Top tick: rejection block short filled")
alertcondition(aInval, "RB invalidated", "Rejection block invalidated before entry")

// ============================ STATS TABLE ====================================
var table stat = na
if barstate.islast and showStats
    tblPos = switch statsPos
        "Top Right"    => position.top_right
        "Top Left"     => position.top_left
        "Bottom Right" => position.bottom_right
        "Bottom Left"  => position.bottom_left
        "Middle Right" => position.middle_right
        => position.top_right
    if na(stat)
        stat := table.new(tblPos, 5, 29, border_width=1, frame_color=color.new(color.gray, 40), frame_width=1)
    else
        table.set_position(stat, tblPos)
    color hdrBg = color.new(color.gray, 20)
    color rowBg = color.new(color.black, 55)
    color txt   = color.white
    table.clear(stat, 0, 0, 4, 28)
    int live = 0
    if array.size(rbs) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(rbs) - 1
            if not array.get(rbs, i).resolved
                live += 1
    string gapsTxt = onA and onB ? nameA + "/" + nameB : onA ? nameA : onB ? nameB : "off"

    table.cell(stat, 0, 0, "RB " + rbName + " · gaps " + gapsTxt, bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat, 1, 0, "Setups", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat, 2, 0, str.tostring(setups), bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat, 3, 0, "Live", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat, 4, 0, str.tostring(live), bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)

    table.cell(stat, 0, 1, "Daily bias (PXH/PXL)", bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small, tooltip="Powell: from the last daily candle against the one before it. Close above its high = bullish; below its low = bearish; took only the high and closed back inside = bearish; took only the low = bullish; otherwise the candle's color.")
    table.cell(stat, 1, 1, bias == 1 ? "▲ Bull" : bias == -1 ? "▼ Bear" : "-", bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=bias == 1 ? colBull : bias == -1 ? colBear : txt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat, 2, 1, "Order flow", bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small, tooltip="ICT: direction of the last close through a 3-candle swing on gap timeframe A.")
    table.cell(stat, 3, 1, S.ofDir == 1 ? "▲ Bull" : S.ofDir == -1 ? "▼ Bear" : "-", bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=S.ofDir == 1 ? colBull : S.ofDir == -1 ? colBear : txt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat, 4, 1, "≥ " + minGrade, bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small, tooltip="Minimum grade for TOP / BOT markers, alerts, the entry rows and the daily plan.")

    table.cell(stat, 0, 2, "Entry", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat, 1, 2, "Fills", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat, 2, 2, "Fill%", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small, tooltip="Share of finished setups where this entry filled at or above the minimum grade.")
    string tipTp = "Whole position held to that target with the same stop, no breakeven. Average R per filled trade · share of trades that ended above 0R."
    table.cell(stat, 3, 2, "→TP1", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small, tooltip=tipTp)
    table.cell(stat, 4, 2, "→TP2", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small, tooltip=tipTp)
    for m = 0 to 3
        int n = array.get(eFill, m)
        float s1 = array.get(eS1, m)
        float s2 = array.get(eS2, m)
        table.cell(stat, 0, 3 + m, (m == selIdx ? "▶ " : "") + array.get(ENTRY_NAMES, m), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
        table.cell(stat, 1, 3 + m, str.tostring(n), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
        table.cell(stat, 2, 3 + m, f_pct(n, setups), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
        table.cell(stat, 3, 3 + m, fR(s1, array.get(eW1, m), n), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=n > 0 ? (s1 > 0 ? colBull : colBear) : txt, text_size=size.small)
        table.cell(stat, 4, 3 + m, fR(s2, array.get(eW2, m), n), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=n > 0 ? (s2 > 0 ? colBull : colBear) : txt, text_size=size.small)

    int row = 7
    if planOn
        table.cell(stat, 0, row, "Daily plan (▶ → " + planTgt + ")", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small, tooltip="Powell: trade 1 full size, a win ends the day; after a loss trade 2 at ½, then ¼; max " + str.tostring(planMax) + " a day. R is weighted by size.")
        table.cell(stat, 1, row, "Days", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
        table.cell(stat, 2, row, "Green", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small, tooltip="Share of finished plan days that ended above 0R.")
        table.cell(stat, 3, row, "R / day", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
        table.cell(stat, 4, row, "Total", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small, tooltip="Total R of finished plan trades, today's included.")
        float perDay = planDays > 0 ? (planR - (planDay == koDay ? dayR : 0.0)) / planDays : na
        table.cell(stat, 0, row + 1, str.tostring(planN) + " trades · " + f_pct(planW, planN) + " won", bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
        table.cell(stat, 1, row + 1, str.tostring(planDays), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
        table.cell(stat, 2, row + 1, f_pct(planWinD, planDays), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
        table.cell(stat, 3, row + 1, na(perDay) ? "-" : fRs(perDay), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=na(perDay) ? txt : perDay > 0 ? colBull : colBear, text_size=size.small)
        table.cell(stat, 4, row + 1, fRs(planR), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=planR > 0 ? colBull : planR < 0 ? colBear : txt, text_size=size.small)
        string today = not na(planT) ? "Today: in trade " + str.tostring(dayTrades) + " (" + sizeTxt(planT.size) + ")" : dayDone ? (dayR > 0 ? "Today: done, green" : "Today: done, stop trading") : "Today: next trade " + str.tostring(dayTrades + 1) + " at " + sizeTxt(math.pow(0.5, dayTrades))
        table.cell(stat, 0, row + 2, today, bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
        table.cell(stat, 1, row + 2, "", bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
        table.cell(stat, 2, row + 2, "", bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
        table.cell(stat, 3, row + 2, "Today", bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
        table.cell(stat, 4, row + 2, fRs(dayR), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=dayR > 0 ? colBull : dayR < 0 ? colBear : txt, text_size=size.small)
        row += 3

    if fullTbl
        table.cell(stat, 0, row, "Filter lab (▶)", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small, tooltip="Every fill of the selected entry (▶), whatever its grade, split by the factors that held. A factor earns its place if its row beats All fills on a decent sample (about 100 fills).")
        table.cell(stat, 1, row, "Fills", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
        table.cell(stat, 2, row, "Share", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small, tooltip="Share of all fills where this factor held.")
        table.cell(stat, 3, row, "→TP1", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small, tooltip=tipTp)
        table.cell(stat, 4, row, "→TP2", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small, tooltip=tipTp)
        array<string> labNames = array.from("All fills", "PD array (HTF gap)", "Key level / liquidity", "Premium / discount", "Daily bias", "Order flow", "Clean tip", "SMT", "Engineered liquidity", "LTF gap at entry", "OTE", "Displaced", "Session", "Grade A+", "Grade A", "Grade B", "Grade C")
        int nAll = array.get(lN, 0)
        for k = 0 to LAB_N - 1
            int n = array.get(lN, k)
            float s1 = array.get(lS1, k)
            float s2 = array.get(lS2, k)
            bool off = k == 7 and not smtOn
            table.cell(stat, 0, row + 1 + k, array.get(labNames, k), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
            table.cell(stat, 1, row + 1 + k, off ? "off" : str.tostring(n), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
            table.cell(stat, 2, row + 1 + k, off ? "" : f_pct(n, nAll), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
            table.cell(stat, 3, row + 1 + k, off ? "" : fR(s1, array.get(lW1, k), n), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=n > 0 ? (s1 > 0 ? colBull : colBear) : txt, text_size=size.small)
            table.cell(stat, 4, row + 1 + k, off ? "" : fR(s2, array.get(lW2, k), n), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=n > 0 ? (s2 > 0 ? colBull : colBear) : txt, text_size=size.small)
